+\subsection{Data Processing Path}
+Every result in the paper is produced by the same locked path. A scenario group samples the public-proxy target or hard-negative family, site, range band, aspect, noise/clutter regime, and phase schedule. Each group then expands into phase records, synthetic IQ/cue products are generated, detector-view summaries are materialized, audit-only columns are blocked by the model-facing denylist, and baselines plus EI read only the permitted detector-view scores. The holdout split is group-locked before any candidate discovery, so phase records from one scenario group cannot appear on both sides of training and evaluation.
+
+Figure~\ref{fig:datapipeline} shows that the model never consumes hidden generator state, labels, split identifiers, group identifiers, raw arrays, or measured files. Those fields exist for audit and reproducibility, but the scoring path sees only detector-facing summaries. This distinction is critical: the paper's claim is not that the generator is physically complete; it is that the declared synthetic signal chain, data processing, split locks, and score outputs are reviewable.
+
